      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__trigger__block_1a9f59b34b1f25fe00023291b678246bcc" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int length</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>length</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_trigger_block::length</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Length in multiples of the device main clock period (3.2ns). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>It corresponds to the total amount of data that is recorded in addition to the trigger window. <ref refid="structndigo__trigger__block_1aa313c7cca7f719735e68839e5f9ec632" kindref="member">precursor</ref> determines how many of these are ahead of the trigger and how many are appended after the trigger.</para>
<para>In edge trigger mode (see <ref refid="structndigo__trigger_1a27316febd6206386bbbc8e1310678962" kindref="member">ndigo_trigger::edge</ref>), the trigger window is always one main clock cycle wide.</para>
<para>In level trigger mode it is as long as the trigger condition is fulfilled.</para>
<para>The length setting is ignored for the TDC channel. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_common_interface.h" line="748" column="9" bodyfile="ndigo_common_interface.h" bodystart="748" bodyend="-1"/>
